ssues.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Decision quality good, attention good, but communication poor, egocentric, not adaptable.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as loner. Good problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to start discussion, maybe propose candidate B as leading due to reliability and stress handling, despite communication concerns. Or candidate D? Let's pick B as initial recommendation, argue strengths and note concerns.\n\nPublic message: state recommendation for Candidate B, reference discussion (none yet) but we can say \"Based on the facts we have\". Provide evidence: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), excellent computer skills (technical). Acknowledge concerns: pretentious, wrong tone (communication). Conclude that strengths outweigh concerns, still best overall.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
